# API keys for the optional cloud model. Copy this file to .env.local (git ignores it) and fill in your own key:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# Then restart (npm start). With a key, "ElevenLabs Scribe v2 Realtime (cloud)" appears in the Model menu.
# The desktop app reads .env.local from its data folder instead:
#   macOS:   ~/Library/Application Support/Live Transcriber/.env.local
#   Windows: %APPDATA%\Live Transcriber\.env.local
# Any other setting from the README's environment-variable table can go here too; real environment variables win.

# ElevenLabs: https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys (a key with access to Speech to Text is enough).
# With this model the speech is sent to ElevenLabs, which bills each second it receives.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Optional: another ElevenLabs region (data residency), e.g. https://api.eu.residency.elevenlabs.io
# ELEVENLABS_BASE_URL=
